SUBENT        23661001   20260331   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                 14         71
TITLE      Cross section measurements of neutron elastic and
            inelastic scattering on 54Fe
AUTHOR     (G.Gkatis, M.Diakaki, G.Noguere, M.Nyman, A.Oprea,
            C.Paradela, E.Pirovano, A.J.M.Plompen)
INSTITUTE  (2FR CAD,2GRCTUA,2SF HLS,2ZZZGEL,2GERPTB)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,109,034612,2024)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.109.034612
           (R,INDC(EUR)-0042,2026)
           #doi:10.61092/iaea.3e74-pjcw
            Details on Legendre coefficient determination
FACILITY   (LINAC,2ZZZGEL) GELINA
INC-SOURCE (PHOTO)
            GELINA:
             Nominal average beam energy:  100 MeV
             Nominal average peak current:  35 uA
             Repetition rate:              400 Hz
             Pulse width:          typically 1 ns (FWHM)
             Primary neutron production target:
                U-Mo alloy with 10wt% of Mo, depleted uranium
             Moderator:
                Unmoderated flux configuration
             Flight path direction:
                108 deg from the electron beam direction
             Neutron beam diameter at sample: 4.9(2) cm
SAMPLE     Enriched iron disk
            Thickness:     0.0106(2) at/b
            Sample mass:     19.494(10) g
            Surface dimension: 51.00(51) mm diam.x1.30(1) mm thick
           (26-FE-54,ENR=0.9768)
           (26-FE-56,ENR=0.0224)
           (26-FE-57,ENR=0.0004)
           (26-FE-58,ENR=0.0004)
METHOD     (TOF)
            GELINA:
             Source-scattering distance:      27.037(5) m
             Source-fission chamber distance: 25.667(5) m
             TOF resolution:                          5 ns
             Energy resolution (at 1 MeV):            5 keV
DETECTOR   (SCIN) EJ301 and EJ315 liquid organic scintillators,
            (cylindrical, 5.08 cm diam.x5.08 cm high, 105.9 cm3),
             which front face is placed at a distance of
             0.300(3) m from the center of the sample.
            Four detectors (two in horizontal, two at 60 deg with
             the horizontal plane facing downward) at each of the
             following angles (deg):
              163.8(1), 142.8(1), 121.7(1), 100.6(1), 79.4(1),
              58.3(1), 37.2(1), 16.2(1).
            The scintillator absolute neutron response was
             determined in a TOF experiment using carbon (neutron
             elastic scattering cross section standard) as
             scattering sample.
           (FISCH) UF4 deposited on Al (8 deposits of 70 mm diam.,
            4.095(4) mg/cm2)
CORRECTION - Dead time
           - Background subtraction
             . Photon-induced events discriminated via pulse
               shape analysis
             . Neutron background - room return neutron
               determination and sample-in/sample-out
               measurements
           - Multiple scattering
               Correction factor determined via Monte Carlo
               simulations.
           - Elastic/inelastic reaction separation
               via neutron spectrometry (deconvolution of the
               detector response).
MONITOR    (92-U-235(N,F),,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (,,3,ENDF/B-VIII.0,,2018)
STATUS     (TABLE) Data received from Georgios Gkatis
HISTORY    (20240403C) Georgios Gkatis
           (20260331A) On. 006+007 added. Major rev. in 002-005.
ENDBIB              71
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           74
